"A duality between pairs of split decompositions for a $Q$-polynomial distance-regular graph (https://arxiv.org/abs/0705.0167)\nciteturn1academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 19.5 years ago; Title: A duality between pairs of split decompositions for a $Q$-polynomial distance-regular graph ... In this paper we show that the ($\\downarrow,\\downarrow$)--split decomposition and the ($\\uparrow,\\uparrow$)--split decomposition are dual with respect to the standard Hermitian form on $V$.\nTitle: A duality between pairs of split decompositions for a $Q$-polynomial distance-regular graph\nAuthors: Joohyung Kim\nDate: Tue May  1 20:12:21 2007\n\nLet $\\Gamma$ denote a $Q$-polynomial distance-regular graph with diameter $D \\geq 3$ and standard module $V$. Recently Ito and Terwilliger introduced four direct sum decompositions of $V$; we call these the $(\\mu,\\nu)$--{\\it split decompositions} of $V$, where $\\mu, \\nu \\in \\lbrace \\downarrow, \\uparrow \\rbrace$. In this paper we show that the ($\\downarrow,\\downarrow$)--split decomposition and the ($\\uparrow,\\uparrow$)--split decomposition are dual with respect to the standard Hermitian form on $V$. We also show that the ($\\downarrow,\\uparrow$)--split decomposition and the ($\\uparrow,\\downarrow$)--split decomposition are dual with respect to the standard Hermitian form on $V$.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA duality between pairs of split decompositions for a Q-polynomial distance-regular graph (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/222678424_A_duality_between_pairs_of_split_decompositions_for_a_Q-polynomial_distance-regular_graph)\nciteturn1search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 16.4 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; # A duality between pairs of split decompositions for a Q-polynomial distance-regular graph ... In this paper we show that the (↓,↓)-split decomposition and the (↑,↑)-split decomposition are dual with respect to the standard Hermitian form on V.\n\nArticle\n\n# A duality between pairs of split decompositions for a Q-polynomial distance-regular graph\n\n  * June 2010\n  * Discrete Mathematics 310(12):1828-1834\n\nDOI:10.1016/j.disc.2010.01.004\n\nAuthors:\n\nJoohyung Kim\n\nJoohyung Kim\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nRequest full-text PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research, you can request a copy directly from the author.\n\n## Abstract\n\nLet Γ denote a Q-polynomial distance-regular graph with diameter D≥3 and standard module V. Recently, Ito and Terwilliger introduced four direct sum decompositions of V; we call these the (μ,ν)-split decompositions of V, where μ,ν∈{↓,↑}. In this paper we show that the (↓,↓)-split decomposition and the (↑,↑)-split decomposition are dual with respect to the standard Hermitian form on V. We also show that the (↓,↑)-split decomposition and the (↑,↓)-split decomposition are dual with respect to the standard Hermitian form on V.\n\n\n## No full-text available\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research,\nyou can request a copy directly from the author.\n\nRequest full-text PDF\n\n## Citations (13)\n\n## References (28)--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndblp: Discrete Mathematics, Volume 310 (https://dblp.org/db/journals/dm/dm310.html)\nciteturn1search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; A duality between pairs of split decompositions for a Q-polynomial distance-regular graph.\n      * RDF Turtle\n      * RDF/XML\n      * XML\n      * plain text\n\ndblp key:\n\n      * journals/dm/Kim10b\n\n    * ask others\n\n      * Google\n      * Google Scholar\n      * Semantic Scholar\n      * Internet Archive Scholar\n      * CiteSeerX\n      * PubPeer\n\n    * share record\n\n      * Bluesky\n      * Reddit\n      * BibSonomy\n      * LinkedIn\n\npersistent URL:\n\n      * https://dblp.org/rec/journals/dm/Kim1